INT. COUNTY PAROLE OFFICE - DAY

Grey light through blinds. Rain on the window. A heater ticks in the corner.

OFFICER DANA REYES sits behind a metal desk. In front of her, ELI COLLINS, 30, in a thrift-store jacket, hands flat on his knees. His younger brother ELLIS stands behind the chair, too close.

The wall clock hums. The rain gets harder.

DANA
Eli, you missed two check-ins.

ELI
Bus broke down. I told the desk.

DANA
The desk says nothing.

ELLIS
He was with me. We walked.

DANA
Ellis, you're not on the list for this meeting.

ELLIS
I'm family.

ELI
Ellis. Sit.

Ellis doesn't. A cheap phone BUZZES on the desk. Dana checks it, frowns, puts it on speaker.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
(over the phone, crackling)
Reyes? Hayes, Fort Dunmore. You've got Collins there?

DANA
Sitting in front of me.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
Tell him the review board turned down the appeal.

Eli stares at the desk. Nothing moves in his face.

ELLIS
What appeal? You said you were done with them.

ELI
I never said that.

NORA, a caseworker in a cardigan, leans in at the door with a folder.

NORA
Dana, sorry, the ten-thirty is early.

DANA
Give us a minute, Nora.

ELLIS
They don't get to decide that. Not after what he did over there.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
Son, nobody's denying what he did.

ELI
Ellis, stop.

ELLIS
They gave him a medal and a record!

NORA
Sir, please lower your voice.

DANA
Mr. Collins, sit down or I'll call it.

ELLIS
Call it! Go ahead!

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
Is somebody shouting?

ELI
(rising, quiet)
Everybody stop.

The room freezes. The heater ticks.

Eli looks at the phone like it's a person.

ELI (CONT'D)
Sergeant. Eleven men walked out of that valley because I did what I did. You remember the number. You signed the paper.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
I remember.

ELI
Then you know what I'm asking for isn't mercy. It's a pen.

SGT. HAYES (V.O.)
The pen isn't mine to lift.

ELI
Then whose is it?

Nobody answers. Rain. The line hisses.

Ellis kicks the chair over. It CRASHES against the wall.

Dana is on her feet. Nora backs into the hallway.

ELLIS
(shaking)
Fifteen months of this. Fifteen months of signing in like a dog.

ELI
Ellis.

DANA
That's enough. Both of you.

Eli puts a hand on his brother's chest. Ellis is breathing hard.

ELI
(soft)
Go wait outside.

Ellis goes. The door shuts. The blinds rattle.

Eli sets the chair upright. Sits. Folds his hands.

ELI (CONT'D)
Sorry about that. What do you need me to sign?
